1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Nf3 Ngf6 6. Nxf6+ Nxf6 7. Bc4 Bf5
8. Qe2 e6 9. Bg5 Be7 10. O-O-O Nd5 11. Bxe7 Qxe7 12. Kb1 Nb4 $5 13. Ne1 Rd8 14.
g4 Bg6 15. Qe5 O-O 16. h4 b5 17. Bb3 Qd6 18. Qxd6 Rxd6 19. h5 Be4 20. f3 Bd5
21. Bxd5 (21. c3 {was simpler}) 21... Nxd5 22. Nd3 $2 Ne3 23. Rde1 Nc4 24. Ne5
{White is lucky not to be dropping a Pawn here, and he needs to find a couple
of inspired moves shortly.} 24... Rxd4 25. Nxc6 Rd6 26. Ne5 Nd2+ 27. Kc1 f6 28.
Re2 $1 Rfd8 ({If} 28... fxe5 29. Rxd2 Rxd2 30. Kxd2 Rxf3 31. Re1 {and Black's
Pawns are just as weak as White's. But what can White do now without losing to
a tactic based on d1?}) 29. Nc6 $1 Rxc6 ({If} 29... R8d7 30. Nb8 Rd8 31. Nc6 {
repeats. Slightly better was damaging White's Pawns with} Nb3+) 30. Rxd2 Rxd2
31. Kxd2 Kf7 32. Re1 e5 33. Re4 Ke6 34. a4 {Now I was confident I could draw
easily} 34... a6 35. axb5 axb5 36. Rb4 Rc5 37. b3 f5 38. c4 fxg4 39. fxg4 bxc4
40. Rxc4 Rb5 41. Rc7 $1 {The simplest. Black can win a Pawn but the
liquidation is too great} 41... Kf6 42. g5+ Kxg5 43. Rxg7+ Kh6 44. Re7 Rxb3 45.
Rxe5 Rh3 1/2-1/2

